{
  "$comment": [
    "Reviewed mapping: PKCS #11 mechanism -> algorithm capability (plan WS-C C-1). ONE file; edits are reviewed like code.",
    "DISCOVERED at runtime (mechanism-inventory.generated.json): which mechanisms each engine lists (C_GetMechanismList), which operations its CKF_ flags make required, and the ulMinKeySize..ulMaxKeySize range (C_GetMechanismInfo).",
    "DECLARED here: algorithm name + revision, PKCS #11 section, enumerated parameter sets (kept only when their keySize falls inside the engine-reported range), sign variants (hedged/deterministic), pre-hash / external-mu / context options, and the length boundaries a boundary case must hit.",
    "Section numbers cite PKCS #11 Specification Version 3.2, OASIS Standard (pkcs11-spec-v3.2-os, 03 June 2026). vendorDefined = a 0x8000xxxx or engine-extension mechanism with no section in that standard. historical = defined only in the PKCS #11 historical-mechanisms document, not the v3.2 base specification.",
    "A mechanism listed by an engine but absent here still produces capability rows (source: discovered-only) and is reported by the coverage gate as unmapped."
  ],
